Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: a nodepool's annotations reach the NodePool

An entry's `annotations:` map is written onto its NodePool's
metadata.annotations as given (toYaml), after the chart's own
argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave. Values must be strings; an entry does not set
the sync-wave. Labels are unchanged: still allowDeletion, maxReplicas and
minReplicas.

The workflows' update-nodepool reads redbull.io/scale-down-policy
(fewest-pods, least-requested, least-utilized) off the NodePool to choose which
servers leave a scale-down; this is how it is written in the values repo.

Without annotations in an entry the render is unchanged: the golden parity
tests pass.

